-- adb (tools/setup/Adb)
VD_SETUP_ADB_GUIDE = "Sending VanillaDroid to the phone with adb (Android Debug Bridge)\n\n1. Developer options: on the phone, Settings > About phone (Samsung: > Software information) and tap Build number seven times.\n2. On this PC, get adb if you do not have it:\n     vdsetup adb setup\n3a. Without a cable (Android 11 or newer, phone and PC on the same Wi-Fi): Settings > Developer options > Wireless debugging, turn it on and open it.\n    Tap \"Pair device with pairing code\": the phone shows an address (IP:port) and a six-digit code.\n     vdsetup adb pair <IP:port> <code>\n    Then, on the Wireless debugging screen, the \"IP address & Port\" (another port):\n     vdsetup adb connect <IP:port>\n3b. With a cable: Settings > Developer options > USB debugging on, connect the phone and accept the question it shows.\n4. Check that the phone is there (state \"device\"):\n     vdsetup adb devices\n   With more than one, choose with --serial <device> (it is remembered).\n5. Install the app and open it once (that makes its folder):\n     vdsetup adb install\n6. Send the game data (only what changed is sent):\n     vdsetup adb push\n7. Optional: send your WoW's archives (5 GB) so the phone can bake updates by itself:\n     vdsetup adb send-wow\n\nXiaomi: also turn on \"Install via USB\" in Developer options.";
